                          69 --27: /* PRQA S 0310,3305 ++ # D002 In order not to disclose the structure used internally,
                          70 --28:                             after receiving it with type uint8_t*, cast it to the type of the structure. */
                          71 --29: /* PRQA S 0311,0316 ++ # D004 The cast needed to pass to the driver API.
                          72 --30:                          There is no problem because it recognizes that the cast value is passed on the driver side. */
                          73 --31: /* PRQA S 1503 ++ # D010 No problem if it is unused because it is an API called from outside the library  */
                          74 --32: /* PRQA S 3383,3384 ++ # D012 Have confirmed in advance that the value doesn't wrap around. */
                          75 --33: /* PRQA S 2981 ++ # D013 Local variable ret of APIs sets INTERNALERR to the initial value
